  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory and map labels the site: G\u00e9nainville.</p>\r\n<div>\u00a0</div>\r\n<div>Some scholars have argued that this site should be identified with the names Petromantalum and Petrum viaco, which appear in the Antonine Itineraries and the Peutinger Map, respectively. <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../114789\">See the separate discussion for details and citations</a>.</div>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient Gallo-Roman sanctuary near modern Genainville (France), with excavated remains of a temple, nymphaeum, and theater: BAtlas 11 B3 G\u00e9nainville (sic)",
